"https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-tw/4-AcO-DMT"},{"title":"维基百科","description":"zh:Encyclopedia article","url":"https://zh.wikipedia.org/zh-cn/4-AcO-DMT"}],"wikidata":"Q3491364","formula":"C14H18N2O2","molarMass":246.3,"pharmacology":{"text":"4-AcO-DMT is a prodrug of psilocin (4-HO-DMT). As a prodrug of psilocin, 4-AcO-DMT acts as a non-selective agonist of serotonin receptors, including of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor. The psychedelic effects of 4-AcO-DMT are mediated specifically by activation of the serotonin 5-HT2A receptor.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"4-AcO-DMT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4-AcO-DMT#Pharmacodynamics","kind":"Non-selective serotonin receptor agonist; Serotonin 5-HT2A receptor agonist; Serotonergic psychedelic; Hallucinogen","body":[{"what":"brokenDown","says":"Deacetylation, others"},{"what":"turnsInto","says":"Psilocin; Psilocin metabolites"}],"figures":"4-AcO-DMT"},"uses":{"text":"The drug is a prodrug of psilocin and is used orally similarly to psilocybin. It was suggested by Nichols as a more economical and accessible alternative to psilocybin for use in scientific research, as the synthesis of psilocybin is more challenging and as psilocybin is a controlled substance. 4-AcO-DMT was first detected as a designer drug in Europe in 2009.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"4-AcO-DMT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4-AcO-DMT","routes":"Oral","figures":"4-AcO-DMT"},"sideEffects":{"text":"4-AcO-DMT, as a prodrug of psilocin, is not expected to differ from psilocybin or psilocin in terms of safety.","source":"Wikipedia","page":"4-AcO-DMT","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/4-AcO-DMT#Side_effects"},"summaryZh":"4-AcO-DMT是一種色胺衍生物，化學式為C14H18N2O2，結構類似物有4-乙醯氧基-N-甲基-N-乙基色胺、4-AcO-DET、4-AcO-MiPT、4-AcO-DiPT。","summaryZhHans":"4-AcO-DMT是一种色胺衍生物，化学式为C14H18N2O2，结构类似物有4-乙酰氧基-N-甲基-N-乙基色胺、4-AcO-DET、4-AcO-MiPT、4-AcO-DiPT。"}